2026-09-24 10:38:46.930 [evictor] WARN  n.a.w.l.c.TenantDynamicRoutingDataSource - [][] Tenant pool test-whse was rebuilt while the previous pool was still closing. The closing pool unregistered this tenant's hikaricp.* meters, so the tenant now publishes none: the series DISAPPEARS rather than reading zero, so a threshold alert stops evaluating instead of firing. No query fails because of this, though the tenant does briefly hold two pools during the overlap. RECOVERY is not the next rebuild, which re-clobbers whenever it overlaps another close; it clears on its own once the tenant stays quiet for wms.tenant.pool.idle-ms (default 15m) and TenantPoolEvictor closes the pool with nothing racing it. To force it sooner, per replica and while that tenant is idle: curl -X POST <host>/actuator/tenantpool -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"tenant":"<t>","facility":"<f>"}' -- the Content-Type is required, a bare POST returns 415. Most frequent causes in order: the 5-minute idle sweep (the only automatic one), that same actuator call, or a landlord config change. SBDEV-3193.
